/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (This SQL problem demonstrates how to classify records into predefined salary categories using the CASE statement and calculate the total number of accounts in each category using the COUNT\(\) aggregate function. It also emphasizes the use of GROUP BY for data summarization and the importance of ensuring that all required categories are displayed, even when a category contains zero records. Overall, the problem strengthens the understanding of conditional logic, aggregation, grouping, and handling edge cases, which are essential skills for writing efficient SQL queries and solving real-world data analysis problems. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
